{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/810459-wolf-paralyzing-stank-bomb","id":810459,"title":"Wolf Paralyzing Stank Bomb","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-16T20:05:16-08:00","id":810459,"title":"Wolf Paralyzing Stank Bomb","content":"I was thinking of a few ways you could attack a werewolf through their supernatural nature, and one method in particular came to mind, smell.<br /> A werewolfs sense of smell is extremely heightened compared to a mortals, so attacking it should be an effective way to incapacitate a were.<br /> <br /> Enter Thioacetone, it is the most odious compound humanity or nature have ever created, a small vial of the stuff exposed to air can be smelled several hundred meters away in seconds, and it causes debilitating nausea and vomiting in humans. It is &quot;lightly studied&quot; because its odor has been described as &quot;fearful.&quot;<br /> <br /> If thats what it does to people, what kind of crippling effects do you think it could have on a Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5016-mobiushero","name":"MobiusHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5016_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T23:28:18-08:00","id":810507,"title":"","content":"Even if you managed to obliterate an Uratha's sense of smell, wolf senses means the other ones instantly compensate, negating any penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T05:21:58-08:00","id":810580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/810459-wolf-paralyzing-stank-bomb?p=810507#post810507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you managed to obliterate an Uratha's sense of smell, wolf senses means the other ones instantly compensate, negating any penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their point is less eliminating their sense of smell as straight up incapacitating them from that smell. If it has such an effect on a human's relatively weak sense of smell, a werewolf might just straight up be down for the count after smelling it. Explosive vomitting, eyes tearing up, vertigo, the works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T05:24:30-08:00","id":810581,"title":"","content":"Maybe apply the Insensate Tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:16:52-08:00","id":810596,"title":"","content":"Then it works best like an attack with toxicity (which is in turn negated by PU).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:22:12-08:00","id":810598,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you have to remember that werewolves hunt Beshilu on a regular basis. A little mortal-made stink bomb? Doesn't even compare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T06:32:48-08:00","id":810600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/810459-wolf-paralyzing-stank-bomb?p=810598#post810598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you have to remember that werewolves hunt Beshilu on a regular basis. A little mortal-made stink bomb? Doesn't even compare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the host haven't been described as being nearly as debilitating as the substance in question, at least in this regard. I don't recall the Beshilu being described as so stinky they drive cities to be evacuated due to the smell. Just because something is mortal made doesn't inherently make it less effective than something supernatural just because it is mortal made.<br /> <br /> Though, as far as mechanics for this type of things are concerned, I'd have it inflict the Insensate Tilt on everyone who can smell it directly, and inflict a scene long Sick Tilt once they leave the stink bombs range. Werewolves would likely have to go much further out to get out of direct smelling range than a normal human would, at least as long as they were using Wolf Senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-17-2016, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T07:41:29-08:00","id":810620,"title":"","content":"The werewolf could just reflexively switch to human senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}